OPC UA binary protocol analyzer
================================

The analyzer registers TCP port 4840 by default and uses a DPD signature for
Hello messages on other ports. Configure additional ports with:

    redef OPCUA::ports += { 4841/tcp };

Supported transport and service messages
----------------------------------------

Transport messages:

* Hello and Acknowledge, including endpoint URL and buffer limits
* OpenSecureChannel request and response
* MSG, CLO, and ABO message chunks
* Continuation (C) and final (F) chunk reassembly

Service messages:

* GetEndpoints
* CreateSession
* Read and Write
* CreateSubscription
* Publish
* ServiceFault

The decoder extracts NodeIds, ExtensionObject type NodeIds, StatusCodes,
endpoint URLs, security policy URIs, security modes, session NodeIds, request
identifiers, and subscription identifiers. NodeIds and ExtensionObject type
NodeIds are bounded by OPCUA::max_node_ids and
OPCUA::max_extension_objects.

Limitations
-----------

* Only unencrypted service bodies are decoded. SignAndEncrypt messages are
  logged with service "Encrypted" after their clear-text transport and
  security headers have been parsed.
* The analyzer decodes the fields needed for audit visibility. It does not
  model complete OPC UA information models, browse paths, method arguments,
  monitored-item filters, or event-filter contents.
* GetEndpoints and CreateSession responses may contain many endpoint
  descriptions. The first description is used for the logged endpoint and
  security policy; the remainder are validated but not emitted individually.
* Abort and CloseSecureChannel support is limited to transport-level
  visibility and headers.
* Messages larger than OPCUA::max_message_size, malformed chunk lengths, and
  TCP gaps stop further parsing for the connection and raise an analyzer
  violation.
